e states why, not what, and SR-236's Requirement and AcceptanceCriteria have carried the dismissal-or-successor resolution since sitting 010 blessed them (re-anchored at act 118). The rationale now argues the obligation the row already imposes; nothing a builder or a test must do moves. No file or carrier is named.\n\nVERDICT: CLARITY rows=2\n\n**Aftermath:** both rows keep their attestation. This session re-anchors them on the released rung, in their own act commit:\n\n`python project-trajectory/scripts/intake.py snapshot --reattests LLR-314,SR-236`\n\nSITTING: JUDGED kinds=amendment\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":994,"cache_read_input_tokens":554023,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":994},"output_tokens":50,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"73ae5cf9-d335-4bb7-a08f-7631da597f26","uuid":"cd5f1e53-b32d-4792-b743-c380134b9183","timestamp":"2026-10-16T04:47:26.319Z","request_id":"req_011Cg5JvFvW2tvNE69uYatnp","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UNheGdFLbDr7w5ut1t5nt6":{"file_path":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-911\\docs\\reviews\\wi-911\\015-ADJUDICATE-3142291.md","content":"# WI-911 adjudication 015: amendment of LLR-314's Detail and SR-236's Rationale\n\nI judged the two cells commit `31422914d` changed. Since act 118 (`f7046f559`) only those two lines moved in the requirement registries (`git diff --stat`: one line each in the SR and LLR files). The SR and LLR rungs are released (`human_approval_through = \"DevStg-Boundary\"`).\n\n## amendment\n\n- [CLARITY] LLR-314 Detail -> parse accepts one reasoned ruling per requested id. The old cell first listed only FIX, DISMISS or ESCALATE, then added \"SUCCESSOR is a fourth ruling: it takes a reason and no