e FIX, DISMISS, or ESCALATE ruling with a reason for every requested id; DISMISS additionally takes only out-of-scope, refuted, or not-worth-cost and a reason. Missing, duplicate, unrequested, malformed, or incomplete content refuses; no value is defaulted. SUCCESSOR is a fourth ruling: it takes a reason and no reason class; an unknown ruling refusal names FIX, SUCCESSOR, DISMISS, and ESCALATE in that order.\"","+detail = \"kitlib.dispute accepts one TOML findings file with only a non-empty `range` and a non-empty `[[finding]]` list. Each finding has exactly a unique letter-led id, held_by `builder` or `coordinator`, and non-empty finding and position text, which the reader keeps verbatim apart from every leading and trailing newline character; spaces and interior lines are kept. request_line writes the composed request, and requested_ids reads its first DISPUTE findings line. parse reads RULING lines one physical line at a time and accepts only one FIX, SUCCESSOR, DISMISS, or ESCALATE ruling with a reason for every requested id; DISMISS additionally takes only out-of-scope, refuted, or not-worth-cost and a reason. Missing, duplicate, unrequested, malformed, or incomplete content refuses; no value is defaulted. SUCCESSOR takes a reason and no reason class; an unknown ruling refusal names FIX, SUCCESSOR, DISMISS, and ESCALATE in that order.\""," rationale = \"Both adjudication routes need one grammar for the coordinator's findings input and the adjudicator's verdict. A single parser prevents a composed brief, entry point, and later loop sitting from accepting different finding sets or verdict meanings.\""," test_refs = \"TC-334\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-911\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\system-requirements.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":1838,"oldLines":7,"newStart":1838,"newLines":7,"lines":[" boundary_refs = [\"B-09\", \"B-10\"]"," hat_refs = [\"UNATTENDED-OPS\"]"," requirement = \"When a reviewed change requires rework, the delivered review workflow shall dispatch that rework only after its plan covers, or excludes with a reason, every finding of the review it answers as a clause in the order written; an exclusion based on a dispute ruling resolves a finding only when an accepted dismissal or successor ruling ruled that same finding.\"","-rationale = \"A DERIVED requirement, and labelled so. SN-024 requires an independent critical eye to drive rework, but does not say how a rework plan preserves every finding that eye raised. The unattended-operations lens listens for a green because nothing looked: dispatching from a plan that omits, renumbers or substitutes a finding lets the change appear answered while the reviewer's concern received no response. Treating every reasoned exclusion as a resolution was rejected because a disputed finding remains open unless its accepted dismissal decided that very finding; keeping each finding as an ordered clause makes the plan and review commensurable. Fed back to the need: SN-024's acceptance could state that rework answers every review finding.\"","+rationale = \"A DERIVED requirement, and labelled so. SN-024 requires an independent critical eye to drive rework, but does not say how a rework plan preserves every finding that eye raised. The unattended-operations lens listens for a green because nothing looked: dispatching from a plan that omits, renumbers or substitutes a finding lets the change appear answered while the reviewer's concern received no response. Treating every reasoned exclusion as a resolution was rejected because a disputed finding remains open unless its accepted dismissal or successor ruling decided that very finding; keeping each finding as an ordered clause makes the plan and review commensurable. Fed back to the need: SN-024's acceptance could state that rework answers every review finding.\""," acceptance_criteria = \"A review verdict or a declared F# findings input produces one ordered clause per finding; dispatch is refused while any clause is neither covered nor reasoned-excluded. An exclusion citing a dispute ruling passes only when its accepted dismissal or successor ruling records the same finding; a dismissal or SUCCESSOR ruling of another finding, another round's same-numbered finding, a finding that cannot be shown, or a ruling other than an accepted DISMISS or SUCCESSOR is refused.\""," priority = \"S\""," verification = \"Test\""]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-911\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-911\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-911\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-911\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\system-requirements.toml"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01B727mR6TEers3AsBRZZ6xz","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
